      "username": "Chief_Lackey_Rich",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/6de8d8/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2023-05-23T16:24:48.059Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Let me save Adam some research if he hasn’t already done it.  Barry Windsor-Smith is still working, although his post-2000 output in comics has been relatively slim.  The most recent thing I’ve seen was his Monsters graphic novel, which came out in 2021 through Fantagraphics - which supposedly started life as a Hulk story, although it became very much its own thing and reached well over 350 pages.  He’s pretty darned active for a 74-year old.</p>\n<p>Assuming his Sentinel Comics equivalent (Larry Hanover-Jones, no doubt) has followed a similar career arc, it’s not impossible that he’d have done the cover art being talked about.  Our version has become a lot more selective about what work he’ll take and how much creative control he insists on, so it’s possible negotiations fell through, though.</p>",
